    },
    {
      "text": "A and B only",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A: Cis - But-2-ene</p><p>B: Trans - But-2-ene</p><p>More polar molecules are more soluble in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. Hence A &gt;B.</p><p>Molecules having higher dipole moments have higher boiling points due to larger intermolecular&nbsp;forces of attraction.&nbsp;More symmetric isomers have higher melting points due to better packing in crystalline lattice &amp; trans isomers are more symmetric than cis. Hence, in case of boiling point it is A&gt;B and in case of melting point it is B&gt;A.</p><p>cis-isomer has resultant of dipoles while in trans isomer dipole moments cancel out.&nbsp;</p><p>So, the correct answer is B, C and D only.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}